<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE softwarecomponent PUBLIC "-//JTRS//DTD SCA V2.2.2 SCD//EN" "softwarecomponent.dtd">
<!--
  Software Component Descriptor (SCD) for the MANET_Node SCA Resource.

  COMPONENT BOUNDARY: this descriptor wraps the assembled node (hh_node_t,
  include/hhsdr/manet/node.h), not the individual internal modules
  (Discovery/Neighbor/LinkHealth/FailureDetector/Topology/Routing/
  SelfHealing). Those seven modules are wired to each other exclusively
  through an in-process event dispatcher (src/core/dispatcher.c) using direct
  C struct calls -- never CORBA, never inter-process -- so they are not
  separate SCA component boundaries today. src/sca/resource.c's per-module
  classification table remains the correct content basis for a *future*,
  finer-grained decomposition (see docs/SCA-COMPATIBILITY.md open item 4:
  "each mesh node being a full SCA domain" is explicitly unresolved); this
  phase wraps the one boundary the C code actually has.

  PORTS: derived only from hh_node_t's real external entry points
  (include/hhsdr/manet/node.h) and the radio contract it depends on
  (include/hhsdr/radio/radio.h):

    - hh_node_on_frame(node, frame, metrics)   -- inbound path: a frame plus
      its measured link sample arrives from the radio/SDR boundary. This is
      the same HTI-04/HTI-05 pairing the radio vtable documents
      ("both are properties of the same reception").
    - hh_radio_transmit() via hh_forwarder / hh_node's owned hh_radio_t --
      outbound path: framed messages (beacon, data, routing) leave toward
      the radio/SDR boundary (HTI-03).
    - hh_node_send(node, dst, payload, len, now) -- application data
      injected into the MANET stack for delivery (data-plane payload, not a
      radio frame; the node's forwarder frames it internally).
    - hh_telemetry_node_status() / hh_telemetry_dump() (telemetry.h) --
      read-only status export, off the fast path, matching the
      ManagementTelemetry Service classification in src/sca/resource.c.

  No RF/IQ/sample-level port exists here: HH_RADIO_MAX_FRAME/hh_frame_t is
  framed data, not baseband samples (radio.h is explicit that this is a
  deliberate boundary choice). A future OpenCPI/FPGA integration attaches
  BELOW the Radio/SDR Interface boundary this component's uses-port faces,
  per docs/diagrams/redhawk-opencpi-integration.drawio -- that integration is
  explicitly out of scope for this phase.

  IDL repIds below use a placeholder namespace (IDL:HHSDR/MANET/...) because
  no IDL module defining frame/status/config structures has been authored or
  compiled in this repository. This SCD intentionally names ports and
  directions without inventing a working IDL binding -- see the "AMBIGUITIES"
  note at the end of this file.
-->
<softwarecomponent>

  <corbaversion>2.2</corbaversion>
  <componentrepid repid="IDL:CF/Resource:1.0"/>
  <componenttype>resource</componenttype>

  <componentfeatures>
    <supportsinterface repid="IDL:CF/LifeCycle:1.0" supportsname="LifeCycle"/>
    <supportsinterface repid="IDL:CF/TestableObject:1.0" supportsname="TestableObject"/>
    <supportsinterface repid="IDL:CF/PropertySet:1.0" supportsname="PropertySet"/>
    <supportsinterface repid="IDL:CF/PortSupplier:1.0" supportsname="PortSupplier"/>
    <supportsinterface repid="IDL:CF/Resource:1.0" supportsname="Resource"/>

    <ports>
      <!-- Inbound: framed reception + measured link metrics from the
           Radio/SDR Interface boundary (radio.h hh_radio_rx_fn, HTI-04/05). -->
      <provides repid="IDL:HHSDR/MANET/FrameConsumer:1.0" providesname="radio_frame_in">
        <description>
          Inbound path for hh_node_on_frame(): one over-the-air frame
          (hh_frame_t, radio.h) plus the hh_link_sample_t metrics measured for
          it. Pairs HTI-04 (DiscoveryBeacon receipt) and HTI-05 (link metric
          sample) exactly as the radio adapter reports them together.
        </description>
      </provides>

      <!-- Outbound: framed transmission toward the Radio/SDR Interface
           boundary (HTI-03). -->
      <uses repid="IDL:HHSDR/MANET/FrameProducer:1.0" usesname="radio_frame_out">
        <description>
          Outbound path used by the Packet Forwarder and control-plane
          components (Discovery beacons, Routing updates, data-plane frames)
          to hand a framed message (hh_frame_t) to the radio/SDR boundary via
          hh_radio_transmit(). Also carries HTI-14 channel_control requests
          (hh_radio_set_channel) issued by Self-Healing, since both are
          operations on the same hh_radio_t contract this component depends
          on -- not a separate port, because the C code does not separate
          them.
        </description>
      </uses>

      <!-- Application data plane: opaque payload in/out via hh_node_send(). -->
      <provides repid="IDL:HHSDR/MANET/DataConsumer:1.0" providesname="app_data_in">
        <description>
          Inbound path for hh_node_send(node, dst, payload, len, now):
          opaque application payload to be delivered toward a MANET
          destination node id. This is a distinct entry point from
          radio_frame_in -- payload here has not yet been framed.
        </description>
      </provides>

      <!-- Read-only management/telemetry export (Service-classified in
           src/sca/resource.c; never on the forwarding path). -->
      <provides repid="IDL:HHSDR/MANET/StatusQuery:1.0" providesname="status_out">
        <description>
          Read-only export of hh_node_status_t (telemetry.h) and the
          formatted neighbor/route/topology reports
          (hh_telemetry_format_*()). Matches the ManagementTelemetry Service
          classification: no mandated CF::Resource lifecycle of its own,
          read-only, off the critical path.
        </description>
      </provides>
    </ports>
  </componentfeatures>

  <interfaces>
    <interface repid="IDL:CF/LifeCycle:1.0" name="LifeCycle"/>
    <interface repid="IDL:CF/TestableObject:1.0" name="TestableObject"/>
    <interface repid="IDL:CF/PropertySet:1.0" name="PropertySet"/>
    <interface repid="IDL:CF/PortSupplier:1.0" name="PortSupplier"/>
    <interface repid="IDL:CF/Resource:1.0" name="Resource"/>
  </interfaces>

</softwarecomponent>

<!--
  AMBIGUITIES:

  1. No compiled IDL exists in this repository for frame/status/config
     structures (docs/SCA-COMPATIBILITY.md gap #2: "the HW/SW spec supplies
     IDL struct definitions; no IDL compiler output or ORB binding exists").
     The repIds above (IDL:HHSDR/MANET/*) name the port *semantics* this
     component actually has without inventing a binding for data that has no
     IDL today. Authoring HHSDR.idl (structs for hh_frame_t, hh_link_sample_t,
     hh_node_status_t, and the CF::Properties mapping for hh_config_t) is
     required before these ports can be realized as real CORBA ports, and is
     left for a follow-up phase rather than invented here.

  2. hh_forwarder_t (dataplane/forwarder.c) is explicitly OUTSIDE the SCA
     Resource graph per src/sca/resource.c and its own header comment
     ("deliberately OUTSIDE the SCA Resource graph ... sub-microsecond
     forwarding-path timing"). This SCD nonetheless exposes radio_frame_out
     as a single uses-port for the whole node, because from the perspective
     of anything outside hh_node_t, the forwarder's transmissions and the
     control plane's beacon/routing transmissions leave through the same
     hh_radio_t the node owns -- there is no separate external seam between
     them today. A future finer-grained decomposition (ambiguity noted in the
     header above) would need to decide whether the fast path gets its own
     port with different QoS/threading assumptions.

  3. RadioSdrInterface is classified HH_SCA_DEVICE in src/sca/resource.c
     ("Owned by the Device Manager, not the Application"). This SCD does not
     attempt to describe that Device or its DCD/DeviceManager relationship --
     out of scope per explicit instruction (no DomainManager/DeviceManager/
     Application deployment in this phase). radio_frame_in/radio_frame_out
     above describe only the boundary this component presents outward; what
     sits on the other side of that boundary is not this file's concern.
-->
